\section{The next idea}
\label{sec:next-idea}

Notes-only structure goes in \verb|\mode<article>{...}|; slide-only
tweaks go in \verb|\mode<presentation>{...}|.  A \verb|\clearpage| before
a section drains the \verb|\ltnote| queue on a page still inside the
chapter.

\begin{frame}
  \begin{summary}
    A block that closes a section by summarising it is a
    \texttt{summary}, not a \texttt{remark} --- and the prose does not
    pre-announce what it is about to say.
  \end{summary}
\end{frame}
